{"test_id": "B14-016", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B14", "input": {"question": "**Gap:** Third-party assets not tracked\n**Sector:** Healthcare CII\n\nProvide a remediation recommendation that addresses:\n1. Specific actions to remediate the gap\n2. Feasibility assessment (cost, timeline, disruption, capability)\n3. Practical considerations for implementation\n4. Alternatives if primary remediation is not feasible", "scenario_sector": "healthcare", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "non-compliant", "expected_response": "**Remediation Recommendation for: Third-party assets not tracked**\n\n**Sector Context:** Healthcare CII\n\n**Recommended Actions:**\nThird-party asset inventory: 1) Vendor survey for connected assets, 2) Network scan for vendor connections, 3) Contract review for asset requirements, 4) Update asset register, 5) Include in vulnerability management.\n\n**Feasibility Assessment:**\n- **Cost:** Medium\n- **Timeline:** 3-4 months\n- **Operational Disruption:** Low\n- **Implementation Capability:** In-House\n\n**Key Considerations:**\n- Vendor cooperation required for complete inventory (critical priority)\n- Contract enforcement may be needed for compliance (important priority)\n- Vulnerability scanning must account for third-party assets (important priority)\n\n\n**Alternative Approaches (if primary not feasible):**\n- Consider compensating controls if primary remediation infeasible\n- Phased implementation to manage operational impact\n- Risk acceptance with formal documentation for gaps that cannot be remediated\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management and control implementation principles", "key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP 2.0 requires remediation of identified gaps", "source": "CCoP 2.0", "tier": "important"}, {"fact": "Remediation feasibility must consider operational constraints", "source": "CCoP principles", "tier": "supporting"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Dismissing feasibility challenges", "Proposing infeasible solutions as straightforward", "Ignoring sector-specific constraints", "Missing: Specific remediation actions", "Missing: Feasibility assessment", "Missing: Practical implementation considerations"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vendor products or solutions", "Creating unrealistic timelines or costs"]}, "metadata": {"section": "6", "clause_reference": ["6.1.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "remediation_scenario", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B14-017", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B14", "input": {"question": "**Gap:** IT/OT convergence unmanaged\n**Sector:** Water CII\n\nProvide a remediation recommendation that addresses:\n1. Specific actions to remediate the gap\n2. Feasibility assessment (cost, timeline, disruption, capability)\n3. Practical considerations for implementation\n4. Alternatives if primary remediation is not feasible", "scenario_sector": "water", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "non-compliant", "expected_response": "**Remediation Recommendation for: IT/OT convergence unmanaged**\n\n**Sector Context:** Water CII\n\n**Recommended Actions:**\nArchitecture review and controls: 1) Map all IT/OT connections, 2) Security architecture review, 3) Implement DMZ between IT and OT, 4) Establish change management for new connections, 5) Monitor cross-boundary traffic.\n\n**Feasibility Assessment:**\n- **Cost:** High\n- **Timeline:** 6-9 months\n- **Operational Disruption:** Medium\n- **Implementation Capability:** Consultant Required\n\n**Key Considerations:**\n- Architecture review requires specialized IT/OT security expertise (critical priority)\n- DMZ implementation provides controlled boundary without operational disruption (critical priority)\n- Change management prevents future unmanaged convergence (important priority)\n\n\n**Alternative Approaches (if primary not feasible):**\n- Consider compensating controls if primary remediation infeasible\n- Phased implementation to manage operational impact\n- Risk acceptance with formal documentation for gaps that cannot be remediated\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management and control implementation principles", "key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP 2.0 requires remediation of identified gaps", "source": "CCoP 2.0", "tier": "important"}, {"fact": "Remediation feasibility must consider operational constraints", "source": "CCoP principles", "tier": "supporting"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Dismissing feasibility challenges", "Proposing infeasible solutions as straightforward", "Ignoring sector-specific constraints", "Missing: Specific remediation actions", "Missing: Feasibility assessment", "Missing: Practical implementation considerations"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vendor products or solutions", "Creating unrealistic timelines or costs"]}, "metadata": {"section": "6", "clause_reference": ["6.1.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "remediation_scenario", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B14-018", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B14", "input": {"question": "**Gap:** Backup restoration never tested\n**Sector:** Government CII\n\nProvide a remediation recommendation that addresses:\n1. Specific actions to remediate the gap\n2. Feasibility assessment (cost, timeline, disruption, capability)\n3. Practical considerations for implementation\n4. Alternatives if primary remediation is not feasible", "scenario_sector": "government", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "non-compliant", "expected_response": "**Remediation Recommendation for: Backup restoration never tested**\n\n**Sector Context:** Government CII\n\n**Recommended Actions:**\nRestoration testing program: 1) Prioritize critical systems, 2) Schedule quarterly tests, 3) Document RTO/RPO achievement, 4) Update backup strategy based on results, 5) Executive sign-off on test results.\n\n**Feasibility Assessment:**\n- **Cost:** Medium\n- **Timeline:** 6-9 months\n- **Operational Disruption:** Medium\n- **Implementation Capability:** Mixed\n\n**Key Considerations:**\n- Testing requires scheduled downtime affecting operations (critical priority)\n- Phased approach by criticality manages disruption (important priority)\n- Failed tests may require backup strategy redesign (important priority)\n\n\n**Alternative Approaches (if primary not feasible):**\n- Consider compensating controls if primary remediation infeasible\n- Phased implementation to manage operational impact\n- Risk acceptance with formal documentation for gaps that cannot be remediated\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management and control implementation principles", "key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP 2.0 requires remediation of identified gaps", "source": "CCoP 2.0", "tier": "important"}, {"fact": "Remediation feasibility must consider operational constraints", "source": "CCoP principles", "tier": "supporting"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Dismissing feasibility challenges", "Proposing infeasible solutions as straightforward", "Ignoring sector-specific constraints", "Missing: Specific remediation actions", "Missing: Feasibility assessment", "Missing: Practical implementation considerations"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vendor products or solutions", "Creating unrealistic timelines or costs"]}, "metadata": {"section": "6", "clause_reference": ["6.1.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "remediation_scenario", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B14-019", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B14", "input": {"question": "**Gap:** Service accounts over-privileged\n**Sector:** Banking CII\n\nProvide a remediation recommendation that addresses:\n1. Specific actions to remediate the gap\n2. Feasibility assessment (cost, timeline, disruption, capability)\n3. Practical considerations for implementation\n4. Alternatives if primary remediation is not feasible", "scenario_sector": "banking", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "non-compliant", "expected_response": "**Remediation Recommendation for: Service accounts over-privileged**\n\n**Sector Context:** Banking CII\n\n**Recommended Actions:**\nService account remediation: 1) Inventory all service accounts, 2) Identify actual requirements for each, 3) Create role-specific accounts, 4) Remove excessive privileges, 5) Implement rotation where possible.\n\n**Feasibility Assessment:**\n- **Cost:** Medium\n- **Timeline:** 4-6 months\n- **Operational Disruption:** High\n- **Implementation Capability:** In-House\n\n**Key Considerations:**\n- Risk of service disruption during privilege reduction (critical priority)\n- Application testing required for each privilege change (critical priority)\n- Phased approach with rollback capability minimizes disruption (important priority)\n\n\n**Alternative Approaches (if primary not feasible):**\n- Consider compensating controls if primary remediation infeasible\n- Phased implementation to manage operational impact\n- Risk acceptance with formal documentation for gaps that cannot be remediated\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management and control implementation principles", "key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP 2.0 requires remediation of identified gaps", "source": "CCoP 2.0", "tier": "important"}, {"fact": "Remediation feasibility must consider operational constraints", "source": "CCoP principles", "tier": "supporting"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Dismissing feasibility challenges", "Proposing infeasible solutions as straightforward", "Ignoring sector-specific constraints", "Missing: Specific remediation actions", "Missing: Feasibility assessment", "Missing: Practical implementation considerations"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vendor products or solutions", "Creating unrealistic timelines or costs"]}, "metadata": {"section": "6", "clause_reference": ["6.1.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "remediation_scenario", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B14-020", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B14", "input": {"question": "**Gap:** Physical access controls weak\n**Sector:** Energy CII\n\nProvide a remediation recommendation that addresses:\n1. Specific actions to remediate the gap\n2. Feasibility assessment (cost, timeline, disruption, capability)\n3. Practical considerations for implementation\n4. Alternatives if primary remediation is not feasible", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "non-compliant", "expected_response": "**Remediation Recommendation for: Physical access controls weak**\n\n**Sector Context:** Energy CII\n\n**Recommended Actions:**\nPhysical security upgrade: 1) Man-trap installation at data center, 2) Enhanced camera coverage, 3) Visitor escort policy enforcement, 4) Badge access logging and review, 5) Security guard presence during business hours.\n\n**Feasibility Assessment:**\n- **Cost:** High\n- **Timeline:** 4-6 months\n- **Operational Disruption:** Medium\n- **Implementation Capability:** Vendor Required\n\n**Key Considerations:**\n- Physical security upgrades require capital investment (critical priority)\n- Man-trap installation may require facility modification (important priority)\n- Policy enforcement requires cultural change (important priority)\n\n\n**Alternative Approaches (if primary not feasible):**\n- Consider compensating controls if primary remediation infeasible\n- Phased implementation to manage operational impact\n- Risk acceptance with formal documentation for gaps that cannot be remediated\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management and control implementation principles", "key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP 2.0 requires remediation of identified gaps", "source": "CCoP 2.0", "tier": "important"}, {"fact": "Remediation feasibility must consider operational constraints", "source": "CCoP principles", "tier": "supporting"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Dismissing feasibility challenges", "Proposing infeasible solutions as straightforward", "Ignoring sector-specific constraints", "Missing: Specific remediation actions", "Missing: Feasibility assessment", "Missing: Practical implementation considerations"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vendor products or solutions", "Creating unrealistic timelines or costs"]}, "metadata": {"section": "6", "clause_reference": ["6.1.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "remediation_scenario", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B14-021", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B14", "input": {"question": "**Gap:** No network segmentation between zones\n**Sector:** Healthcare CII\n\nProvide a remediation recommendation that addresses:\n1. Specific actions to remediate the gap\n2. Feasibility assessment (cost, timeline, disruption, capability)\n3. Practical considerations for implementation\n4. Alternatives if primary remediation is not feasible", "scenario_sector": "healthcare", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "non-compliant", "expected_response": "**Remediation Recommendation for: No network segmentation between zones**\n\n**Sector Context:** Healthcare CII\n\n**Recommended Actions:**\nNetwork segmentation project: 1) Zone definition by sensitivity, 2) Firewall deployment between zones, 3) Rule development and testing, 4) Gradual migration, 5) Monitoring of cross-zone traffic.\n\n**Feasibility Assessment:**\n- **Cost:** High\n- **Timeline:** 9-12 months\n- **Operational Disruption:** High\n- **Implementation Capability:** Vendor Required\n\n**Key Considerations:**\n- Major infrastructure project requiring significant planning (critical priority)\n- Phased migration manages operational risk (critical priority)\n- Zone definitions must align with business requirements (important priority)\n\n\n**Alternative Approaches (if primary not feasible):**\n- Consider compensating controls if primary remediation infeasible\n- Phased implementation to manage operational impact\n- Risk acceptance with formal documentation for gaps that cannot be remediated\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management and control implementation principles", "key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP 2.0 requires remediation of identified gaps", "source": "CCoP 2.0", "tier": "important"}, {"fact": "Remediation feasibility must consider operational constraints", "source": "CCoP principles", "tier": "supporting"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Dismissing feasibility challenges", "Proposing infeasible solutions as straightforward", "Ignoring sector-specific constraints", "Missing: Specific remediation actions", "Missing: Feasibility assessment", "Missing: Practical implementation considerations"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vendor products or solutions", "Creating unrealistic timelines or costs"]}, "metadata": {"section": "6", "clause_reference": ["6.1.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "remediation_scenario", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B14-022", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B14", "input": {"question": "**Gap:** OT SCADA system end-of-life\n**Sector:** Water CII\n\nProvide a remediation recommendation that addresses:\n1. Specific actions to remediate the gap\n2. Feasibility assessment (cost, timeline, disruption, capability)\n3. Practical considerations for implementation\n4. Alternatives if primary remediation is not feasible", "scenario_sector": "water", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "non-compliant", "expected_response": "**Remediation Recommendation for: OT SCADA system end-of-life**\n\n**Sector Context:** Water CII\n\n**Recommended Actions:**\nEnd-of-life system management: 1) Risk acceptance with compensating controls (network isolation, monitoring), 2) Migration planning for replacement, 3) Budget allocation for replacement, 4) Interim security controls, 5) Vendor engagement for extended support if available.\n\n**Feasibility Assessment:**\n- **Cost:** Very_High\n- **Timeline:** 24-36 months\n- **Operational Disruption:** Very_High\n- **Implementation Capability:** Vendor Required\n\n**Key Considerations:**\n- System replacement requires multi-year capital planning (critical priority)\n- Compensating controls manage risk during extended timeline (critical priority)\n- Risk acceptance formal documentation required for regulators (important priority)\n\n\n**Alternative Approaches (if primary not feasible):**\n- Consider compensating controls if primary remediation infeasible\n- Phased implementation to manage operational impact\n- Risk acceptance with formal documentation for gaps that cannot be remediated\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management and control implementation principles", "key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP 2.0 requires remediation of identified gaps", "source": "CCoP 2.0", "tier": "important"}, {"fact": "Remediation feasibility must consider operational constraints", "source": "CCoP principles", "tier": "supporting"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Dismissing feasibility challenges", "Proposing infeasible solutions as straightforward", "Ignoring sector-specific constraints", "Missing: Specific remediation actions", "Missing: Feasibility assessment", "Missing: Practical implementation considerations"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vendor products or solutions", "Creating unrealistic timelines or costs"]}, "metadata": {"section": "6", "clause_reference": ["6.1.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "remediation_scenario", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B14-023", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B14", "input": {"question": "**Gap:** OT system vendor out of business\n**Sector:** Energy CII\n\nProvide a remediation recommendation that addresses:\n1. Specific actions to remediate the gap\n2. Feasibility assessment (cost, timeline, disruption, capability)\n3. Practical considerations for implementation\n4. Alternatives if primary remediation is not feasible", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "non-compliant", "expected_response": "**Remediation Recommendation for: OT system vendor out of business**\n\n**Sector Context:** Energy CII\n\n**Recommended Actions:**\nUnsupported OT system: 1) Maximum isolation from networks, 2) Compensating controls (monitoring, access restrictions), 3) Replacement evaluation and planning, 4) Consider third-party maintenance, 5) Risk assessment and acceptance documentation.\n\n**Feasibility Assessment:**\n- **Cost:** Very_High\n- **Timeline:** 18-24 months\n- **Operational Disruption:** Very_High\n- **Implementation Capability:** Consultant Required\n\n**Key Considerations:**\n- No vendor support available for patches or vulnerabilities (critical priority)\n- Replacement may require system redesign not just swap (critical priority)\n- Regulatory engagement may be needed for risk acceptance (critical priority)\n\n\n**Alternative Approaches (if primary not feasible):**\n- Consider compensating controls if primary remediation infeasible\n- Phased implementation to manage operational impact\n- Risk acceptance with formal documentation for gaps that cannot be remediated\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management and control implementation principles", "key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP 2.0 requires remediation of identified gaps", "source": "CCoP 2.0", "tier": "important"}, {"fact": "Remediation feasibility must consider operational constraints", "source": "CCoP principles", "tier": "supporting"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Dismissing feasibility challenges", "Proposing infeasible solutions as straightforward", "Ignoring sector-specific constraints", "Missing: Specific remediation actions", "Missing: Feasibility assessment", "Missing: Practical implementation considerations"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vendor products or solutions", "Creating unrealistic timelines or costs"]}, "metadata": {"section": "6", "clause_reference": ["6.1.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "remediation_scenario", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B14-024", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B14", "input": {"question": "**Gap:** No intrusion prevention system budget\n**Sector:** Government CII\n\nProvide a remediation recommendation that addresses:\n1. Specific actions to remediate the gap\n2. Feasibility assessment (cost, timeline, disruption, capability)\n3. Practical considerations for implementation\n4. Alternatives if primary remediation is not feasible", "scenario_sector": "government", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "non-compliant", "expected_response": "**Remediation Recommendation for: No intrusion prevention system budget**\n\n**Sector Context:** Government CII\n\n**Recommended Actions:**\nBudget-constrained IPS alternative: 1) Enhance IDS capabilities with better alerting, 2) Implement network segmentation to contain threats, 3) Use cloud-based security services, 4) Optimize existing firewall rules, 5) Budget request for next fiscal year.\n\n**Feasibility Assessment:**\n- **Cost:** Low\n- **Timeline:** 3-6 months\n- **Operational Disruption:** Low\n- **Implementation Capability:** In-House\n\n**Key Considerations:**\n- Compensating controls provide partial coverage when primary control unaffordable (critical priority)\n- Cloud services may offer cost-effective alternative (important priority)\n- Budget request requires business case with risk quantification (important priority)\n\n\n**Alternative Approaches (if primary not feasible):**\n- Consider compensating controls if primary remediation infeasible\n- Phased implementation to manage operational impact\n- Risk acceptance with formal documentation for gaps that cannot be remediated\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management and control implementation principles", "key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP 2.0 requires remediation of identified gaps", "source": "CCoP 2.0", "tier": "important"}, {"fact": "Remediation feasibility must consider operational constraints", "source": "CCoP principles", "tier": "supporting"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Dismissing feasibility challenges", "Proposing infeasible solutions as straightforward", "Ignoring sector-specific constraints", "Missing: Specific remediation actions", "Missing: Feasibility assessment", "Missing: Practical implementation considerations"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vendor products or solutions", "Creating unrealistic timelines or costs"]}, "metadata": {"section": "6", "clause_reference": ["6.1.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "remediation_scenario", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B14-025", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B14", "input": {"question": "**Gap:** Small team cannot implement all controls\n**Sector:** Water CII\n\nProvide a remediation recommendation that addresses:\n1. Specific actions to remediate the gap\n2. Feasibility assessment (cost, timeline, disruption, capability)\n3. Practical considerations for implementation\n4. Alternatives if primary remediation is not feasible", "scenario_sector": "water", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "non-compliant", "expected_response": "**Remediation Recommendation for: Small team cannot implement all controls**\n\n**Sector Context:** Water CII\n\n**Recommended Actions:**\nResource-constrained prioritization: 1) Risk-based prioritization of gaps, 2) Implement quick wins first, 3) Leverage managed security services, 4) Seek peer collaboration or consortium options, 5) Request additional headcount with ROI justification.\n\n**Feasibility Assessment:**\n- **Cost:** Medium\n- **Timeline:** 12-18 months\n- **Operational Disruption:** Low\n- **Implementation Capability:** External Msp\n\n**Key Considerations:**\n- Small team requires prioritization and external support (critical priority)\n- Managed services can augment limited internal capability (critical priority)\n- Consortium approaches may provide cost sharing opportunities (supporting priority)\n\n\n**Alternative Approaches (if primary not feasible):**\n- Consider compensating controls if primary remediation infeasible\n- Phased implementation to manage operational impact\n- Risk acceptance with formal documentation for gaps that cannot be remediated\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management and control implementation principles", "key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP 2.0 requires remediation of identified gaps", "source": "CCoP 2.0", "tier": "important"}, {"fact": "Remediation feasibility must consider operational constraints", "source": "CCoP principles", "tier": "supporting"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Dismissing feasibility challenges", "Proposing infeasible solutions as straightforward", "Ignoring sector-specific constraints", "Missing: Specific remediation actions", "Missing: Feasibility assessment", "Missing: Practical implementation considerations"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vendor products or solutions", "Creating unrealistic timelines or costs"]}, "metadata": {"section": "6", "clause_reference": ["6.1.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "remediation_scenario", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B14-026", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B14", "input": {"question": "**Gap:** Zero budget increase available\n**Sector:** Government CII\n\nProvide a remediation recommendation that addresses:\n1. Specific actions to remediate the gap\n2. Feasibility assessment (cost, timeline, disruption, capability)\n3. Practical considerations for implementation\n4. Alternatives if primary remediation is not feasible", "scenario_sector": "government", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "non-compliant", "expected_response": "**Remediation Recommendation for: Zero budget increase available**\n\n**Sector Context:** Government CII\n\n**Recommended Actions:**\nZero-budget remediation: 1) Process-only changes (policy updates, documentation), 2) Configuration optimizations (no new tools), 3) Reallocate existing budget, 4) Leverage open-source tools, 5) Seek grant funding or government programs.\n\n**Feasibility Assessment:**\n- **Cost:** Low\n- **Timeline:** 6-12 months\n- **Operational Disruption:** Low\n- **Implementation Capability:** In-House\n\n**Key Considerations:**\n- Process improvements provide security without capital investment (critical priority)\n- Configuration optimization extracts more value from existing tools (important priority)\n- Government cybersecurity grants may be available (supporting priority)\n\n\n**Alternative Approaches (if primary not feasible):**\n- Consider compensating controls if primary remediation infeasible\n- Phased implementation to manage operational impact\n- Risk acceptance with formal documentation for gaps that cannot be remediated\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management and control implementation principles", "key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP 2.0 requires remediation of identified gaps", "source": "CCoP 2.0", "tier": "important"}, {"fact": "Remediation feasibility must consider operational constraints", "source": "CCoP principles", "tier": "supporting"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Dismissing feasibility challenges", "Proposing infeasible solutions as straightforward", "Ignoring sector-specific constraints", "Missing: Specific remediation actions", "Missing: Feasibility assessment", "Missing: Practical implementation considerations"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vendor products or solutions", "Creating unrealistic timelines or costs"]}, "metadata": {"section": "6", "clause_reference": ["6.1.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "remediation_scenario", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B14-027", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B14", "input": {"question": "**Gap:** Contractor access without time limits\n**Sector:** Telecommunications CII\n\nProvide a remediation recommendation that addresses:\n1. Specific actions to remediate the gap\n2. Feasibility assessment (cost, timeline, disruption, capability)\n3. Practical considerations for implementation\n4. Alternatives if primary remediation is not feasible", "scenario_sector": "telecoms", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "non-compliant", "expected_response": "**Remediation Recommendation for: Contractor access without time limits**\n\n**Sector Context:** Telecommunications CII\n\n**Recommended Actions:**\nContractor access management: 1) Implement time-limited accounts with auto-expiry, 2) Sponsor requirement for contractor access, 3) Regular access review, 4) Justification for extensions, 5) Monitoring of contractor activity.\n\n**Feasibility Assessment:**\n- **Cost:** Medium\n- **Timeline:** 2-3 months\n- **Operational Disruption:** Medium\n- **Implementation Capability:** In-House\n\n**Key Considerations:**\n- Process changes can be implemented quickly with management support (critical priority)\n- Auto-expiry requires identity management system capability (important priority)\n- Sponsor accountability creates enforcement mechanism (important priority)\n\n\n**Alternative Approaches (if primary not feasible):**\n- Consider compensating controls if primary remediation infeasible\n- Phased implementation to manage operational impact\n- Risk acceptance with formal documentation for gaps that cannot be remediated\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management and control implementation principles", "key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP 2.0 requires remediation of identified gaps", "source": "CCoP 2.0", "tier": "important"}, {"fact": "Remediation feasibility must consider operational constraints", "source": "CCoP principles", "tier": "supporting"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Dismissing feasibility challenges", "Proposing infeasible solutions as straightforward", "Ignoring sector-specific constraints", "Missing: Specific remediation actions", "Missing: Feasibility assessment", "Missing: Practical implementation considerations"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vendor products or solutions", "Creating unrealistic timelines or costs"]}, "metadata": {"section": "6", "clause_reference": ["6.1.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "remediation_scenario", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B14-028", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B14", "input": {"question": "**Gap:** Database encryption not implemented (high volume)\n**Sector:** Banking CII\n\nProvide a remediation recommendation that addresses:\n1. Specific actions to remediate the gap\n2. Feasibility assessment (cost, timeline, disruption, capability)\n3. Practical considerations for implementation\n4. Alternatives if primary remediation is not feasible", "scenario_sector": "banking", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "non-compliant", "expected_response": "**Remediation Recommendation for: Database encryption not implemented (high volume)**\n\n**Sector Context:** Banking CII\n\n**Recommended Actions:**\nDatabase encryption for high-volume systems: 1) Performance impact assessment, 2) Transparent data encryption (TDE) evaluation, 3) Hardware security module (HSM) consideration, 4) Phased implementation by database, 5) Performance testing after encryption.\n\n**Feasibility Assessment:**\n- **Cost:** High\n- **Timeline:** 9-12 months\n- **Operational Disruption:** Medium\n- **Implementation Capability:** Vendor Required\n\n**Key Considerations:**\n- Encryption may impact database performance significantly (critical priority)\n- Phased implementation manages performance risk (critical priority)\n- HSM may be required for key management compliance (important priority)\n\n\n**Alternative Approaches (if primary not feasible):**\n- Consider compensating controls if primary remediation infeasible\n- Phased implementation to manage operational impact\n- Risk acceptance with formal documentation for gaps that cannot be remediated\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management and control implementation principles", "key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP 2.0 requires remediation of identified gaps", "source": "CCoP 2.0", "tier": "important"}, {"fact": "Remediation feasibility must consider operational constraints", "source": "CCoP principles", "tier": "supporting"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Dismissing feasibility challenges", "Proposing infeasible solutions as straightforward", "Ignoring sector-specific constraints", "Missing: Specific remediation actions", "Missing: Feasibility assessment", "Missing: Practical implementation considerations"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vendor products or solutions", "Creating unrealistic timelines or costs"]}, "metadata": {"section": "6", "clause_reference": ["6.1.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "remediation_scenario", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B14-029", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B14", "input": {"question": "**Gap:** Legacy protocols in OT cannot be upgraded\n**Sector:** Transportation CII\n\nProvide a remediation recommendation that addresses:\n1. Specific actions to remediate the gap\n2. Feasibility assessment (cost, timeline, disruption, capability)\n3. Practical considerations for implementation\n4. Alternatives if primary remediation is not feasible", "scenario_sector": "transport", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "non-compliant", "expected_response": "**Remediation Recommendation for: Legacy protocols in OT cannot be upgraded**\n\n**Sector Context:** Transportation CII\n\n**Recommended Actions:**\nLegacy protocol mitigation: 1) Network isolation using firewalls, 2) Protocol gateways for translation, 3) Deep packet inspection for anomaly detection, 4) Monitor for protocol exploitation attempts, 5) Plan system replacement long-term.\n\n**Feasibility Assessment:**\n- **Cost:** High\n- **Timeline:** 12-24 months\n- **Operational Disruption:** Low\n- **Implementation Capability:** Vendor Required\n\n**Key Considerations:**\n- Legacy protocols cannot be secured without system replacement (critical priority)\n- Compensating controls provide defense-in-depth (critical priority)\n- Protocol gateways add latency but enable monitoring (important priority)\n\n\n**Alternative Approaches (if primary not feasible):**\n- Consider compensating controls if primary remediation infeasible\n- Phased implementation to manage operational impact\n- Risk acceptance with formal documentation for gaps that cannot be remediated\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management and control implementation principles", "key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP 2.0 requires remediation of identified gaps", "source": "CCoP 2.0", "tier": "important"}, {"fact": "Remediation feasibility must consider operational constraints", "source": "CCoP principles", "tier": "supporting"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Dismissing feasibility challenges", "Proposing infeasible solutions as straightforward", "Ignoring sector-specific constraints", "Missing: Specific remediation actions", "Missing: Feasibility assessment", "Missing: Practical implementation considerations"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vendor products or solutions", "Creating unrealistic timelines or costs"]}, "metadata": {"section": "6", "clause_reference": ["6.1.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "remediation_scenario", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B14-030", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B14", "input": {"question": "**Gap:** Multiple critical gaps with safety-critical operations\n**Sector:** Energy CII\n\nProvide a remediation recommendation that addresses:\n1. Specific actions to remediate the gap\n2. Feasibility assessment (cost, timeline, disruption, capability)\n3. Practical considerations for implementation\n4. Alternatives if primary remediation is not feasible", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "non-compliant", "expected_response": "**Remediation Recommendation for: Multiple critical gaps with safety-critical operations**\n\n**Sector Context:** Energy CII\n\n**Recommended Actions:**\nSafety-critical remediation: 1) Quick wins that don't affect operations, 2) Compensating controls for high-impact fixes, 3) Schedule high-impact work during planned outages, 4) Safety case for each remediation, 5) Regulator engagement for timeline.\n\n**Feasibility Assessment:**\n- **Cost:** Very_High\n- **Timeline:** 24-36 months\n- **Operational Disruption:** Very_High\n- **Implementation Capability:** Expert Consultant\n\n**Key Considerations:**\n- Safety-critical systems require special consideration for any changes (critical priority)\n- Compensating controls enable progress without safety impact (critical priority)\n- Regulator communication essential for extended remediation timelines (critical priority)\n\n\n**Alternative Approaches (if primary not feasible):**\n- Consider compensating controls if primary remediation infeasible\n- Phased implementation to manage operational impact\n- Risk acceptance with formal documentation for gaps that cannot be remediated\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management and control implementation principles", "key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP 2.0 requires remediation of identified gaps", "source": "CCoP 2.0", "tier": "important"}, {"fact": "Remediation feasibility must consider operational constraints", "source": "CCoP principles", "tier": "supporting"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Dismissing feasibility challenges", "Proposing infeasible solutions as straightforward", "Ignoring sector-specific constraints", "Missing: Specific remediation actions", "Missing: Feasibility assessment", "Missing: Practical implementation considerations"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vendor products or solutions", "Creating unrealistic timelines or costs"]}, "metadata": {"section": "6", "clause_reference": ["6.1.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "remediation_scenario", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
